        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An anti-gravity treadmill uses air pressure in a sealed chamber to hold you at a set
            fraction of your body weight while your gait stays essentially normal.
            <strong class="text-white">It turns running from a threshold into a dial</strong>, which
            is genuinely valuable for a graded return from injury.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            You book one rather than buy one — ask your clinician whether it suits your injury, and use
            the manufacturer's location finder. If what you want is low-impact training at home,
            <a href="/best-incline-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">a treadmill with real incline</a>
            gets you a surprising distance toward the same trade for a tiny fraction of the money.
          </p>
